From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:48:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: Enable the video mode BTA on VLV/CHV
 (diagnostic)

EXPERIMENT, diagnostic only, not for upstream.

With DISABLE_VIDEO_BTA set (from the VBT on a GPD Win 1) the host never
turns the bus around in video mode, so the panel can never report
receive errors (SoT/EoT sync, ECC, checksum: MIPI_INTR_STAT bits 0-13,
24-26 per the VLV PRM). Clear the bit so the panel gets a BTA at the last
VFP line and its acknowledge becomes visible, to learn whether the panel
sees errors when the picture loses alignment.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
index 877eab7..8f5911c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -1478,6 +1478,15 @@ static void intel_dsi_prepare(struct intel_encoder *encoder,
 		if (is_vid_mode(intel_dsi)) {
 			u32 fmt = intel_dsi->video_frmt_cfg_bits | IP_TG_CONFIG;
 
+			/*
+			 * EXPERIMENT (diagnostic): allow the bus turnaround at
+			 * the last VFP line, so that the panel's acknowledge
+			 * with error report shows up in MIPI_INTR_STAT bits
+			 * 0-13 and 24-26 (receiver SoT/EoT sync errors etc).
+			 */
+			if (display->platform.valleyview || display->platform.cherryview)
+				fmt &= ~DISABLE_VIDEO_BTA;
+
 			/*
 			 * Some panels might have resolution which is not a
 			 * multiple of 64 like 1366 x 768. Enable RANDOM
